{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"95","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Horse Races"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya likes horse racing very much. Horses numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" take part in the races. Petya wants to evaluate the probability of victory; for some reason, to do that he needs to know the amount of nearly lucky horses' numbers. A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nearly lucky"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number is an integer number that has at least two lucky digits the distance between which does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":". Petya learned from some of his mates from Lviv that lucky digits are digits "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":". The distance between the digits is the absolute difference between their positions in the number of a horse. For example, if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", then numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"412395497"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"404"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4070400000070004007"},{"kind":"text","text":" are nearly lucky and numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"k